("CDC's reprocessing methods for heat-resistant instruments from high-infectivity CJD tissue begin with which step?",
 "Soaking in 1N sodium hydroxide", ["A standard enzyme presoak", "A routine flash cycle", "Wiping with 70% alcohol"],
 "CDC's methods immerse the instruments in 1N sodium hydroxide (or sodium hypochlorite in some methods), then autoclave, clean and sterilize routinely. CDC still calls destroying them the safest option."),
("Which tissue does CDC list as low infectivity for Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease?",
 "Cerebrospinal fluid", ["Brain", "Eye", "Spinal cord"],
 "CDC lists brain, spinal cord and eyes as high infectivity, and cerebrospinal fluid, kidney, liver, lung, lymph nodes, spleen and placenta as low infectivity."),
